WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.220
If the onboarding page does not start automatically, go to the bottom left to Applications, Accessories, Jibian Onboarding.

00:08.020 --> 00:11.940
Once launched, click on “Configure your OpenPGP security key”.

00:12.460 --> 00:12.980
I confirm.

00:13.440 --> 00:14.240
Do you have a key? Yes.

00:14.460 --> 00:14.960
Insert it.

00:15.640 --> 00:16.100
Select Yes.

00:16.340 --> 00:17.000
It is detected.

00:17.300 --> 00:17.740
Continue.

00:17.920 --> 00:18.960
Do you have the QR codes? No.

00:19.200 --> 00:21.260
Create my OpenPGP identity.

00:21.360 --> 00:21.880
I confirm.

00:22.340 --> 00:28.040
Enter your birth name, given names, date of birth, and finally your country of birth.

00:29.440 --> 00:29.880
Continue.

00:30.460 --> 00:32.240
Here, enter your email address.

00:34.100 --> 00:35.240
Then continue.

00:35.560 --> 00:36.520
Check your information.

00:37.140 --> 00:37.620
Continue.

00:38.120 --> 00:39.380
Click on Print.

00:39.540 --> 00:40.680
Print your QR codes.

00:40.860 --> 00:42.540
Once this is done, click on Continue.

00:42.700 --> 00:43.280
I confirm.

00:43.380 --> 00:44.660
You can see that your key is detected.

00:44.780 --> 00:45.260
Continue.

00:45.620 --> 00:46.720
Do you have the QR codes? Yes.

00:47.100 --> 00:47.600
Scan them.

00:48.200 --> 00:51.380
Here you can see the first one, the second one, and the last one.

00:53.760 --> 00:54.160
Save.

00:54.340 --> 00:55.280
And that’s it, your key is created.
